{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 44, :comments ["<b>As the bees do.</b> Rashi explained: just as this bee, when it strikes a person, immediately dies — that is, it dies from the effort of striking the person, because of the weakness in it — so too they, even though they are weak, for always when they touched you they would immediately die — even so, they struck you in Seir as far as Hormah. Another interpretation: <b>as the bees do</b> — if one leaves its place, they all follow after it; so too, 'the Amalekite and the Canaanite came down,' etc." "<b>And they struck you.</b> Struck and wounded, but did not kill them, so that the name of HaShem would not be profaned by magnifying the mouth of their enemies against them. You know this, for Scripture did not count the fallen in this war, as it did in other wars."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:51:55.425982803Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}